    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "If the area of a circle is divided by 9, what happens to the radius? What happens to the circumference?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "The radius and circumference are both divided by 3.",
      "worked": "Area is proportional to the square of the radius. Dividing the radius by 3 divides the area by $3^2=9$. Since $C=2\\pi r$, the circumference is also divided by 3.",
